---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = '25 September 2026';
---

<Base
  title="Terms — Nudgy"
  description="The terms for using Nudgy."
  path="/terms"
>
  <main class="prose">
    <h1>Terms</h1>
    <p class="faint">Last updated {updated}</p>

    <p>
      Nudgy is made by Pragmatic Labs. These terms are short because the product is small and there is
      currently nothing to pay for.
    </p>

    <h2>Using Nudgy</h2>
    <p>
      You need an account, and you’re responsible for what happens under it. Don’t use Nudgy to store
      information about people in ways that would be illegal where you live.
    </p>

    <h2>Information about other people</h2>
    <p>
      Nudgy is for personal use — your own relationships. The people you add haven’t agreed to be in it, so
      treat what you write with the care you’d want applied to notes about you. Don’t use Nudgy to build
      profiles of people for resale, surveillance, or harassment.
    </p>

    <h2>It’s in development</h2>
    <p>
      Nudgy is being actively built. Things will change, break, and occasionally be unavailable. Keep your own
      copy of anything you can’t afford to lose — Settings → Export everything gives you all of it as a file.
    </p>

    <h2>Money</h2>
    <p>
      Nudgy is currently free and there is nothing to buy. If that changes, you’ll be told before it affects
      you, and nothing you already have will be taken away without notice.
    </p>

    <h2>Ending it</h2>
    <p>
      You can delete your account at any time from Settings, and everything goes with it. We may close
      accounts that are being used to harm people, and we’ll tell you why if we do.
    </p>

    <h2>The legal part</h2>
    <p>
      Nudgy is provided as-is, without warranties. To the extent the law allows, Pragmatic Labs isn’t liable
      for losses arising from using it — including anything that happens because a reminder didn’t arrive.
      Nudgy is a memory aid, not a guarantee.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p><a href="mailto:hello@pragmaticlabs.dev">hello@pragmaticlabs.dev</a></p>

    <footer>
      <a href="/">Nudgy</a>
      <a href="/privacy">Privacy</a>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
